From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL DO NOT SUBMIT v3] drm/nouveau: probe HDMI RGB deep colour
 with GCP declaration + wire-state instrumentation

Hardware-discovery patch, revision 3, for the GA106 -> KDL-46HX855
controlled test. Includes everything from v2 (do not stack).

Run 3 measured that adding the GCP declaration alone is still not
sufficient: the sink returned the same "incompatible signal" OSD.
Cross-checking NVIDIA's own evo3 code (nvkms-evo3.c) afterwards showed
every visible method we send now matches their recipe bit for bit:
head OUTPUT_RESOURCE PIXEL_DEPTH=36_444 (the field that actually carries
depth on C37D/C57D cores; the class SOR_SET_CONTROL has no PIXEL_DEPTH
field, and Nouveau's sorc37d_ctrl never merges the NV837D depth bits, so
run 2/3 matched NVIDIA there too), plus the GCP subpack/control writes.
NVKMS sends nothing rate-related for TMDS deep colour anywhere open, and
its SET_HDMI_SINK_CAPS RM call carries no deep-colour bits.

The remaining split is therefore: (a) the CPU-side GCP MMIO write does
not stick under GSP ownership of that aperture [inferred], or (b) the
TMDS character rate never rises to 222.75 MHz because the GSP RM clock
derivation needs some state nouveau does not provide [inferred].

v3 adds read-only instrumentation to split them on the next run:
gv100_sor_hdmi_gcp() prints the written subpack plus readbacks of the
 GCP subpack, GCP control, and the sibling AVI control/subpack registers;
 nv50_sor_atomic_enable() prints the selected non-8-bpc TMDS depth.

Base: Debian linux-source 7.0.10 tree, same as v1/v2 builds.
Applies with patch -p1.

